[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115390,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Middle ear adenocarcinoma is a locally aggressive primary epithelial malignancy arising from the middle ear, showing glandular differentiation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115391,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8260/3 Middle ear adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115392,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C21.0 Adenocarcinoma of middle ear</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115393,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> papillary adenocarcinoma of middle ear; low-grade adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> endolymphatic sac tumour (distinct tumour category); aggressive papillary tumour of middle ear.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115394,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115395,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour extensively fills the middle ear and/or tympanic cavity, expanding into the petrous bone apex, sometimes involving the cerebellopontine angle and cerebellum {18633929}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115396,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p >Described mostly in case reports {8692411; 11307613; 14738614; 17167601; 18633929; 32940914}, symptoms are often of a long duration and nonspecific; they include hearing loss, otalgia, vestibular dysfunction, and otorrhoea.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-16T17:27:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115397,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The age range at presentation is broad (16&ndash;55&nbsp;years, median: 33&nbsp;years, mean: 34&nbsp;years), but given the long symptom duration, the age at onset may be younger. There is a slight female predilection {8692411; 11307613; 14738614; 17167601; 18633929; 32940914}. Isolated cases have been associated with von&nbsp;Hippel&ndash;Lindau syndrome.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115398,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115399,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>VHL</em> mutations have been described in association with aggressive papillary tumours involving middle ear but that involved the endolymphatic sac. Tumours confined to the middle ear without involvement of endolymphatic sac and negative for <em>VHL</em> mutation likely represent a subset of adenocarcinoma distinct from endolymphatic sac tumour. Mouse models of histologically similar tumours showed <em>EGFR</em> mutations {26027747}. Oncocytic and papillary tumours have been reported to have <em>MKRN1</em>::<em>BRAF</em> fusion {32940914}. Tumours resembling salivary polymorphous low-grade adenocarcinoma have been described, but <em>PRKD1</em>, <em>PRKD2</em>, or <em>PRKD3</em> mutation was not proved {34097084}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115400,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The middle ear cleft and mastoid air cells are usually filled with a bone-destructive tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115401,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours show a cystic-papillary glandular pattern with a complex architecture including papillae lying loosely or infiltrating fibrous connective tissue. The papillae are usually lined by a single layer of low cuboidal to columnar epithelial cells with uniform nuclei, eosinophilic cytoplasm, and indistinct cell borders. Thyroid follicle&ndash;like areas may be present, similar to those seen in endolymphatic sac tumour. Appearances similar to oncocytic, mucinous, or polymorphous adenocarcinoma, or even to salivary duct carcinoma, suggest a wide morphological spectrum in these tumours {32940914; 34097084}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry and differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p >Tumour cells are positive for CK7, EMA, and (sometimes) S100. PAX8 and CAIX are negative, unlike in endolymphatic sac tumour {30291511; 32940914}, which is the principal differential consideration. Metastatic carcinomas (lung, thyroid, colon) should be excluded.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-16T17:27:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115402,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115403,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "<p >Not relevant</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-16T17:32:14"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115404,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> imaging confirmation of middle ear localization; a bone-destructive adenocarcinoma, often with papillary growth; exclusion of metastases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115405,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Without standardized staging, International Collaboration on Cancer Reporting (ICCR) minimum data set reporting is encouraged {30500288} [[Thompson LDR, Gupta R, Sandison A, et al. Ear and temporal bone tumours: histopathology reporting guide. 1st ed. Sydney (Australia): International Collaboration on Cancer Reporting; 2018.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 115406,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 300,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis depends on the size of the lesion at presentation and the adequacy of the surgical excision.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T13:29:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]